# The machine that serves this app its bundles over the air (issue #168).
#
# Copy to `.env` and name your own machine. Expo loads `.env` for every one of
# its commands, so `expo prebuild`, the gradle build and `pnpm run export` all
# read the same value — which is the point. Setting it for one step and not
# another produces a binary whose native layer updates and whose JavaScript says
# it cannot; see docs/MOBILE.md.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_` is required: it is what makes Metro inline the value into the
# bundle so `src/ota.ts` reads the same literal `app.config.ts` was built from.
#
# Leave it unset and the app takes no updates over the air, which is the right
# setting for development.
EXPO_PUBLIC_COVEY_UPDATES_URL=http://your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net:3790/updates
